{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Behold, it is for you a covering of eyes.</b> Some say that it is an allusion to the dimness of her son's eyes, and this is the way of derash. The straight interpretation in my eyes is that כסות עינים draws itself and another with it, like \"אל בקצפך תוכיחני\" (Psalms 38:2), and many others. \"הנה הוא לך\" is like \"a covering of eyes\" on account of Abraham, who is your husband. And the meaning of \"let no man lift his eyes to you\" — that too is a covering of eyes for all who are with you, the maidservants who are his servants' wives. The vav of ונוכחת is attached to a patah in the language of Ishmael and in Scripture there are others like it, like \"ביום השלישי וישא אברהם את עיניו\" (Genesis 22:4). And the meaning of ונוכחת according to Moses' words is that Sarah no longer said of Abraham \"he is my brother.\" And הנה is the meaning of ואת כל, and despite all this Sarah was reproved. Some say הנה הוא לך refers to the silver, to buy a garment, and the word נתתי draws itself and another with it, and so it is: הנה נתתי אלף כסף לאחיך — to buy you with it a covering, like כסות, that would be a desire for the eyes; ונתתי לכל אשר אתך; ואת כל — אשר נתתי לאברהם צאן ובקר ועבדים ושפחות. And it is more correct, as I said, that the meaning is that Abraham is a covering of eyes for you and for the servants who are with you who were yours, גם אשר נתתים גם אני." "<b>ואת כל.</b> And with all people, he is for you a covering of eyes." "And ונוכחת according to Moses' words, and the vav stands in its proper place. And the Gaon [Saadia] said it is from נוכח, but his words are not straight."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The phrase 'פ\"א רפה' (soft alef/patah) is rendered as 'a patah,' referring to the furtive patah in ונוכחת where the alef has a hatef-patah rather than a full vowel."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:25.020312949Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}